# Disclosure toolbar panels (anti-clutter)

Owner preference: **secondary filters and view options must not permanently consume vertical space** on phone, tablet, or web.

## Pattern (Markets is the reference)

- Primary toolbar uses exclusive disclosure toggles: **Assets · Timeframe · Format · Filters** (and the same idea elsewhere).
- Opening one panel closes the others.
- Permanent chrome may keep a **single search field** when search is the primary find action.
- Do **not** leave Ownership / Alerts / Freshness / Types (or similar) as always-visible stacked full-width rows under the toolbar.
- Active filters may mark the Filters button (accent border / `--filtered` class) so the user knows something is applied without opening the panel.

## Apply elsewhere

- Prefer the same disclosure style for dense filter clusters on News, YouTube, Spending, Jobs, Todos, etc.
- If a control is only needed sometimes, it belongs in a panel / `⋯` menu / CollapsibleFilters — not a permanent block of selects above the list.

## Never

- Do not reintroduce permanent “All ownership / All alerts / All freshness / All types” rows on Markets.
- Do not add new permanent chip/select strips for secondary filters without an explicit product request that overrides this rule.
